!
! What one care item costs over a month (poultice_rules.h PR4), in
! Trebago, one item per row, exact in integer minor units:
! price * perday * days. A negative value makes ok 0 and the cost a
! division by zero, refused; a product past 64 bits is refused, never
! wrapped. Trebago answers any non-negative row, where cost.sutra holds
! each value to its picture: past them it is held.
trebago carecost
  in  price(n), perday(n), days(n)
  out cost(n)
  var ok(n)
  ok(i) = min(1, max(0, price(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, perday(i) + 1)) &
        * min(1, max(0, days(i) + 1))
  cost(i) = price(i) * perday(i) * days(i) / ok(i)
end
